    "body": "This was probably introduced by the link element updates, but they were not a refactor either really, because they introduced the processing model for `Link`. That's why this doesn't use the usual path, is because it sometimes runs during early hints, where there is no `Document`.\r\n\r\nI agree this reveals that something slipped through when speccing early hints. In particular, which of { early hints , non-early `Link` headers, `<link>` elements } respect a document's encoding during URL resolution? (Does it depend on whether the encoding is delivered via `Content-Type` vs. `<meta charset>`???)\r\n\r\n@noamr is probably the best person to assign to this, indeed. I guess we could avoid blocking this PR, by adding an XXX box of some sort pointing to a tracking issue. I suspect the end result will be that the document's encoding only matters for `<link>` elements, and we'll spec that by adding a new member to link processing options. But having that backed up by tests would be very helpful.",
